   "source": [
    "# Week 4 \u00b7 Topic 2 \u2014 Dictionaries\n",
    "\n",
    "**Box we are building: STORE, with names instead of positions**\n",
    "\n",
    "A list finds things by position. A dictionary finds things by name.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Already know this?** Skip to the *Topic 2 Challenge*."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cbd6c9b3",
   "source": "**Resources**\n\nPython documentation \u2014 [Data Structures: Dictionaries](https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/datastructures.html#dictionaries) \u2014 the official reference, if you want more than this walkthrough covers.",
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 1. Creating and accessing"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "R-001\n",
      "87.0\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "record = {\n",
    "    \"label\": \"R-001\",\n",
    "    \"value\": 87.0,\n",
    "    \"limit\": 100.0,\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "print(record[\"label\"])\n",
    "print(record[\"value\"])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "```\n",
    "record = { \"label\": \"R-001\",  \"value\": 87.0,  \"limit\": 100.0 }\n",
    "\n",
    "record[\"value\"]  \u2500\u2500\u25b6  87.0\n",
    "record[\"missing\"]  \u2500\u2500\u25b6  KeyError\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6e10e756",
   "source": "Animation \u2014 [Dict Lookup](https://anna29.github.io/CST1510/dict_lookup.html) \u2014 open this on the main screen to compare list lookup with dict lookup interactively.",
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Your turn\n",
    "Create a dict for one record with `label`, `value` and `limit`. Print two of its values."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "R-010\n",
      "55.0\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "my_record = {\"label\": \"R-010\", \"value\": 55.0, \"limit\": 100.0}\n",
    "print(my_record[\"label\"])\n",
    "print(my_record[\"value\"])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 2. Adding and updating\n",
    "\n",
    "The same line does both \u2014 if the key exists, it updates; if not, it adds."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "{'label': 'R-001', 'value': 90.0, 'limit': 100.0, 'status': 'OK'}\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "record[\"status\"] = \"OK\"     # new key\n",
    "record[\"value\"] = 90.0       # existing key, updated\n",
    "print(record)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Your turn\n",
    "Add a new key to your dict, then update one of the original ones."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "{'label': 'R-010', 'value': 60.0, 'limit': 100.0, 'status': 'OK'}\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "my_record[\"status\"] = \"OK\"      # new key\n",
    "my_record[\"value\"] = 60.0       # update an existing key\n",
    "print(my_record)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 3. Missing keys, and `.get()`\n",
    "\n",
    "`record[\"missing\"]` raises `KeyError`. `.get()` does not \u2014 it gives you `None`, or a\n",
    "default of your choosing."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "OK\n",
      "None\n",
      "n/a\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(record.get(\"status\"))          # OK\n",
    "print(record.get(\"missing\"))          # None\n",
    "print(record.get(\"missing\", \"n/a\"))    # n/a"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Your turn\n",
    "Use `.get()` to safely check for a key you know does not exist, with a default of your choosing."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "unknown\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(my_record.get(\"owner\", \"unknown\"))   # key does not exist -> default 'unknown'"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 4. Iterating\n",
    "\n",
    "`.items()` gives you both the key and the value together \u2014 the one you will use\n",
    "most."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "label: R-001\n",
      "value: 90.0\n",
      "limit: 100.0\n",
      "status: OK\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "for key, value in record.items():\n",
    "    print(f\"{key}: {value}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Your turn\n",
    "Loop over your dict using `.items()` and print `key: value` for each pair."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "label: R-010\n",
      "value: 60.0\n",
      "limit: 100.0\n",
      "status: OK\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "for key, value in my_record.items():\n",
    "    print(f\"{key}: {value}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b0bef79e",
   "source": "---\n## 5. `zip()` \u2014 building a dict from two lists\n\nSometimes your data starts as two separate lists \u2014 names in one, values in\nanother \u2014 instead of already paired up. `zip()` pairs them together, one from\neach; `dict()` turns those pairs straight into a dictionary.",
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "dfdc5637",
   "source": "hostnames = [\"srv-01\", \"srv-02\", \"srv-03\"]\ndisk_used = [87, 45, 120]\n\npaired = list(zip(hostnames, disk_used))\nprint(paired)     # [('srv-01', 87), ('srv-02', 45), ('srv-03', 120)]\n\nusage = dict(zip(hostnames, disk_used))\nprint(usage)                  # {'srv-01': 87, 'srv-02': 45, 'srv-03': 120}\nprint(usage[\"srv-02\"])         # 45",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "[('srv-01', 87), ('srv-02', 45), ('srv-03', 120)]\n",
      "{'srv-01': 87, 'srv-02': 45, 'srv-03': 120}\n",
      "45\n"
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c797287e",
   "source": "```\nhostnames:   srv-01     srv-02     srv-03\n                \u2502          \u2502          \u2502\ndisk_used:     87         45        120\n                \u2502          \u2502          \u2502\nzip pairs:  (srv-01,87) (srv-02,45) (srv-03,120)\n```\n\nIf the two lists are different lengths, `zip()` stops at the shorter one \u2014\nsilently, with no error.",
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b6c79dbe",
   "source": "### Your turn\nGiven `ips = [\"10.0.0.5\", \"10.0.0.9\", \"10.0.0.12\"]` and `failed = [5, 0, 3]`, build\na dict pairing each IP with its failed-login count, using `zip()`.",
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "35695b75",
   "source": [
    "ips = [\"10.0.0.5\", \"10.0.0.9\", \"10.0.0.12\"]\n",
    "failed = [5, 0, 3]\n",
    "\n",
    "failed_by_ip = dict(zip(ips, failed))\n",
    "print(failed_by_ip)   # {'10.0.0.5': 5, '10.0.0.9': 0, '10.0.0.12': 3}"
   ],
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "{'10.0.0.5': 5, '10.0.0.9': 0, '10.0.0.12': 3}\n"
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 5. Sets \u2014 only unique values, in curly braces too\n",
    "\n",
    "Created with `{a, b, c}` \u2014 or `set()` for an empty one. **Not** `{}`: that makes an\n",
    "empty *dict*, not an empty set. No order, no indexing, and duplicates are dropped\n",
    "automatically."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "{'R-001', 'R-002', 'R-003'}\n",
      "3\n",
      "True\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "labels = [\"R-001\", \"R-002\", \"R-001\", \"R-003\"]\n",
    "unique_labels = set(labels)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(unique_labels)          # duplicates gone\n",
    "print(len(unique_labels))      # 3, not 4\n",
    "print(\"R-001\" in unique_labels)   # True - fast membership check\n",
    "\n",
    "empty_set = set()    # NOT {} - that is an empty dict"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Your turn\n",
    "Given a list with some repeated values, use a set to find out how many unique\n",
    "values it contains."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "{9, 3, 1, 7}\n",
      "4\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "readings = [3, 7, 3, 9, 7, 7, 1]\n",
    "unique_readings = set(readings)\n",
    "print(unique_readings)\n",
    "print(len(unique_readings))   # 4 unique values"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Topic 2 Challenge\n",
    "\n",
    "Given a dict representing one record, print a formatted report line for each\n",
    "key-value pair, right-aligning the values, using `.items()`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "label        R-001\n",
      "value         87.0\n",
      "limit        100.0\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "record = {\"label\": \"R-001\", \"value\": 87.0, \"limit\": 100.0}\n",
    "\n",
    "for key, value in record.items():\n",
    "    print(f\"{key:<8}{str(value):>10}\")   # key left-aligned, value right-aligned"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Same idea, three fields\n",
    "\n",
    "| Field | Looks like |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| **AI / Data Science** | `{\"rows\": 1200, \"missing\": 13, \"source\": \"survey_2026\"}` |\n",
    "| **Cyber Security** | `{\"ip\": \"10.0.0.5\", \"failed\": 12, \"locked\": True}` |\n",
    "| **IT** | `{\"hostname\": \"srv-01\", \"used_gb\": 87, \"total_gb\": 120}` |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "---\n## Common mistakes\n\n| Mistake | What you see | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| `record[\"missing\"]` | `KeyError: 'missing'` | check with `.get()` or `in` first |\n| `record[value]` when you meant `record[\"value\"]` | `NameError` (or wrong result) | keys are strings \u2014 quote them |\n| assuming key order matters for lookup | it doesn't \u2014 lookup is by name, not position | that is the entire point of a dict |\n| `for value in record:` expecting key AND value | only gives you the keys | use `.items()` for both |\n| `{}` expecting an empty set | it is an empty **dict** | use `set()` for an empty set |\n| `zip()`-ing two lists of different lengths | silently stops at the shorter one, no error | check both lists are the same length first |\n\n## Go deeper\n\n`examples/01_creating_and_accessing.py` \u2014 creating, accessing, updating, .get()\n`examples/02_iterating.py` \u2014 .keys(), .values(), .items(), and zip()\n`examples/03_sets.py` \u2014 unique values, membership, the `{}` gotcha"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "---\n## Recap\n\n| You can now | Using |\n|---|---|\n| create a dict | `{\"key\": value, ...}` |\n| access by name | `record[\"key\"]` |\n| add or update | `record[\"key\"] = value` |\n| avoid `KeyError` | `.get(\"key\", default)` |\n| loop over both at once | `.items()` |\n| build a dict from two separate lists | `dict(zip(keys, values))` |\n| keep only unique values | `set(a_list)` |\n\n**Next:** Topic 3 \u2014 storage that outlives the program."
  }
